{%- comment -%}
  GOD SQUAD — grid-sizes
  Phase 12. The product grid's `sizes` attribute, derived once.

  Accepts:
  - cols_d   {Number} required. The desktop column CEILING (Phase 6: the grid is
                      auto-fill with a floor, so this is the most it will paint).
  - cols_t   {Number} required. The tablet ceiling.
  - cols_m   {Number} required. The mobile ceiling.
  - chrome_d {Number} optional, default 96. Horizontal chrome at the desktop
                      tier — gutters plus anything the section puts beside the
                      grid. featured-collection's copy-column preset passes 128.

  Usage:
  {%- capture card_sizes -%}
    {% render 'grid-sizes', cols_d: cols_d, cols_t: cols_t, cols_m: cols_m %}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  WHY THIS IS A SNIPPET AND NOT THREE COPIES.

  It was three copies — featured-collection, main-collection and main-search each
  carried the same ninety lines. Phase 10 found that the desktop clause fired
  below its own breakpoint, booked it as a blocker, and fixed it in
  main-collection. The other two copies kept the bug for two phases, because the
  fix was applied to an instance rather than to the rule. Phase 10's own document
  recorded the duplication as debt; this discharges it.

  TWO CORRECTNESS RULES THIS ENCODES, BOTH LEARNED THE HARD WAY.

  1. A clause may not claim a width before the layout that produces it applies.
     The desktop threshold is derived from column arithmetic alone, so at three
     columns it computes 976 — but the desktop column count does not take effect
     until --bp-lg 1024. Left unfloored, the clause declared 280px for a slot
     painting 452px between 976 and 1023.

  2. A clause may not divide by more columns than actually fit. At the container
     cap the row stops growing, so the track is a fixed pixel value — but the
     grid is auto-fill with a 272px floor, so it paints only as many columns as
     that floor allows. With the shipped maximum of 4 columns and the container
     narrowed to its 1200px minimum, dividing by the REQUESTED 4 declares 253px
     for a track that actually paints 346px: a 27% under-declaration, which makes
     the browser fetch a candidate it then has to upscale.

  Both errors run in the same direction — under-declaring — which is the
  direction that costs image quality.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gap = 32
  comment
    Below --bp-md the grid tightens its column gap to --space-4 16px
    (component-product-card.css) and relaxes its track floor to 8rem. A narrower
    gap makes the cards WIDER, so the mobile clauses have to be computed against
    16 or they under-declare the slot.
  endcomment
  assign gap_m = 16
  assign col_min = 272
  assign col_min_m = 128

  assign chrome_m = 48
  assign chrome_t = 64
  assign chrome_d = chrome_d | default: 96

  assign container = settings.container_width | default: 1440

  comment
    Desktop.
  endcomment
  assign need_d = cols_d | times: col_min
  assign need_d = cols_d | minus: 1 | times: gap | plus: need_d
  assign threshold_d = need_d | plus: chrome_d
  comment
    Rule 1: never claim a width before its layout applies.
  endcomment
  if threshold_d < 1024
    assign threshold_d = 1024
  endif

  assign cols_d_low = cols_d | minus: 1
  if cols_d_low < 1
    assign cols_d_low = 1
  endif

  comment ---------------------------------------------------- tablet
    Does cols_t fit at 768, the tier's own minimum? If not, the tier never
    reaches it, because the next tier starts at 1024.
  endcomment
  assign need_t = cols_t | times: col_min
  assign need_t = cols_t | minus: 1 | times: gap | plus: need_t
  assign row_t_min = 768 | minus: chrome_t
  assign cols_t_used = cols_t
  if need_t > row_t_min
    assign cols_t_used = cols_t | minus: 1
  endif
  if cols_t_used < 1
    assign cols_t_used = 1
  endif

  comment
    Mobile: the floor is 8rem/128px below 768 and the gap is 16px.
  endcomment
  assign need_m = cols_m | times: col_min_m
  assign need_m = cols_m | minus: 1 | times: gap_m | plus: need_m
  assign threshold_m = need_m | plus: chrome_m
  assign cols_m_low = cols_m | minus: 1
  if cols_m_low < 1
    assign cols_m_low = 1
  endif

  assign gaps_d = cols_d | minus: 1 | times: gap
  assign gaps_d_low = cols_d_low | minus: 1 | times: gap
  assign gaps_t = cols_t_used | minus: 1 | times: gap
  assign gaps_m = cols_m | minus: 1 | times: gap_m
  assign gaps_m_low = cols_m_low | minus: 1 | times: gap_m

  comment ------------------------------------------- the capped row
    Above the container cap the row stops growing, so the first clause is a
    fixed pixel value rather than a vw expression.

    Rule 2: divide by what FITS, not by what was asked for. One more column fits
    for every (col_min + gap) of room, once the first column's own width is
    accounted for — so the capacity test adds one gap to the row before dividing.
  endcomment
  assign capped_row = container | minus: chrome_d
  assign col_slot = col_min | plus: gap
  assign fits_d = capped_row | plus: gap | divided_by: col_slot
  if fits_d < 1
    assign fits_d = 1
  endif
  assign cols_capped = cols_d
  if fits_d < cols_d
    assign cols_capped = fits_d
  endif
  assign gaps_capped = cols_capped | minus: 1 | times: gap

  comment
    Integer division truncates, so the cap would be declared one pixel under the
    rendered track; one pixel changes no candidate, but under-declaring is the
    direction that costs quality, so it rounds up.
  endcomment
  assign capped_track = capped_row | minus: gaps_capped | divided_by: cols_capped | plus: 1
-%}
{%- liquid
  echo '(min-width: '
  echo container
  echo 'px) '
  echo capped_track
  echo 'px'

  echo ', (min-width: '
  echo threshold_d
  echo 'px) calc((100vw - '
  echo chrome_d
  echo 'px - '
  echo gaps_d
  echo 'px) / '
  echo cols_d
  echo ')'

  echo ', (min-width: 1024px) calc((100vw - '
  echo chrome_d
  echo 'px - '
  echo gaps_d_low
  echo 'px) / '
  echo cols_d_low
  echo ')'

  echo ', (min-width: 768px) calc((100vw - '
  echo chrome_t
  echo 'px - '
  echo gaps_t
  echo 'px) / '
  echo cols_t_used
  echo ')'

  echo ', (min-width: '
  echo threshold_m
  echo 'px) calc((100vw - '
  echo chrome_m
  echo 'px - '
  echo gaps_m
  echo 'px) / '
  echo cols_m
  echo ')'

  echo ', calc((100vw - '
  echo chrome_m
  echo 'px - '
  echo gaps_m_low
  echo 'px) / '
  echo cols_m_low
  echo ')'
-%}
